      "responsibilities": "<p><br></p><ul><li>Develop, maintain, and enhance core banking applications using Temenos T24/TAFJ.</li><li>Customize and implement application functionalities based on business requirements and technical specifications.</li><li>Develop, maintain, and enhance banking system functionalities using Java and Temenos development tools.</li><li>Analyze business requirements and translate them into technical solutions aligned with banking processes.</li><li>Develop and maintain integrations between Temenos T24 and external systems using APIs, web services, and other integration mechanisms.</li><li>Work with databases to implement data access, queries, and application functionality.</li><li>Troubleshoot, debug, and resolve application issues to ensure system stability and performance.</li><li>Participate in technical discussions, code reviews, and problem-solving activities.</li><li>Perform unit testing and support System Integration Testing (SIT) and User Acceptance Testing (UAT).</li><li>Ensure code quality, maintainability, documentation, and adherence to development standards.</li><li>Support application deployment, production maintenance, incident resolution, and ongoing system improvements.</li><li>Collaborate with business analysts, QA teams, infrastructure teams, and other stakeholders in an Agile/Scrum environment.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>",
      "requirements": "<p><br></p><ul><li>Bachelor's degree in Informatics Engineering, Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field.</li><li>Minimum 3 years of experience in software development, preferably in banking or financial services.</li><li>Strong experience with Temenos T24 / Transact and TAFJ (Temenos Application Framework for Java).</li><li>Good programming skills in Java and experience developing Java-based enterprise applications.</li><li>Understanding of Temenos T24 architecture, application customization, and development processes.</li><li>Experience with Temenos development tools, frameworks, and banking application workflows.</li><li>Experience developing and maintaining system integrations, APIs, and web services.</li><li>Good understanding of relational databases, SQL, and data management.</li><li>Understanding of software development lifecycle, testing, debugging, deployment, and maintenance processes.</li><li>Familiarity with Git or other version control systems.</li><li>Knowledge of core banking processes, such as accounts, deposits, lending, payments, or funds transfers, is an advantage.</li><li>Strong analytical thinking, problem-solving, and debugging skills.</li><li>Good communication and collaboration skills.</li><li>Able to work independently as well as collaboratively within a team.</li><li>Proactive, responsible, and willing to learn and adapt to new technologies.</li><li>Experience working in an Agile/Scrum environment is a plus.</li><li>Open to middle-level candidates with strong hands-on development experience.</li></ul><p><br></p>",
